    "text": "To determine the total cost of Tom's deck, we need to calculate the cost of each type of card and then sum these costs.\n\nFirst, we calculate the cost of the rare cards:\n\\[\n19 \\text{ rare cards} \\times \\$1 \\text{ per rare card} = 19 \\times 1 = \\$19\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the cost of the uncommon cards:\n\\[\n11 \\text{ uncommon cards} \\times \\$0.50 \\text{ per uncommon card} = 11 \\times 0.50 = \\$5.50\n\\]\n\nThen, we calculate the cost of the common cards:\n\\[\n30 \\text{ common cards} \\times \\$0.25 \\text{ per common card} = 30 \\times 0.25 = \\$7.50\n\\]\n\nFinally, we sum the costs of all the cards to find the total cost of the deck:\n\\[\n\\$19 + \\$5.50 + \\$7.50 = \\$32\n\\]\n\nThus, the total cost of Tom's deck is \\(\\boxed{32}\\).",
